  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1156 AM MDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nIt has been another day of sunny but hazy/smokey skies over the \nCWA. The smoke had a little bit of an impact to the air quality \nwith sensors reaching the Moderate stage as of the early \nafternoon. Looking ahead, afternoon temps will be in the 70s to\n80s with continued sunny, buy hazy, skies. Tonight will be calm\nand clear with overnight temps dipping into the 50s to lower 60s.\n\nFor Thursday and Friday, upper level ridging looks to return to\nthe area, which will bring warmer temps and continued mostly dry \nweather. Daily highs will be in the upper 80s to 90s and overnight\nlows will be in the 50s to low 60s. Temps that warm and very\nlittle moisture will cause RH values to drop to around 10 to 20\npercent. A passing front will cause northwest winds to increase \nThursday. That combination of stronger winds and low humidity will\nelevate fire weather conditions. Because of that, a Red Flag\nWarning has been issued. See the Fire Weather section below for\nmore information.\n\nThere are a couple chances for rain on Thursday and again Friday.\nThe previously mentioned front could be the trigger to get some \nthunderstorms going in south-central SD Thursday afternoon. Some \nof those storms could be strong to severe with hail and wind being\nmain concerns if the storms are able to get going. Another round \nof storms is possible Friday night for parts of central SD.\n\nThe 90s and mostly dry weather will last through the weekend with\nhints of slightly cooler weather for the start of next week.\nStorms and severe weather is a concern as the forecasted wind\npattern has been known to produce storms and severe weather and \nmachine learning severe weather models are targeting the Black \nHills with elevated chances of severe storms beginning Saturday.",
